      "en": "Great Grey or Red-backed Shrike?"
    },
    "text": {
      "en": "Great Grey Shrike is a winter bird, big and pale grey, with black wings and a long tail. Red-backed Shrike is a summer bird, smaller, with a rufous back and, in the male, a grey head. A female Red-backed is brown with scaly underparts. Look at the date: a shrike in January is a Great Grey."
